## Context

PR #949 (ticket 0505) found that `experiments/derived/score.mk` was missing
`src/aedist/score_mechanical.py` as a prerequisite of the
`exp1_cross_eval.csv` rule and fixed it there. Review of that PR noted the
same gap exists for `sota_cross_eval.csv`: its scoring path also imports
`score_mechanical.py` (via `score_exp1.py` / `score_ingest.py`), so a change
to `score_mechanical.py` does not trigger a rebuild of `sota_cross_eval.csv`.
Pre-existing debt, out of 0505's scope.

## Actions

1. Verify the actual import chain from the sota scoring entry point to
   `score_mechanical.py`.
2. Add the missing prerequisite(s) to the `sota_cross_eval.csv` rule in
   `experiments/derived/score.mk`; audit sibling rules in the same file for
   the same gap while there (rename-sweep rule: fix the whole logical unit).
3. Regenerate `sota_cross_eval.csv` once to confirm the rule still builds;
   commit only if content changed.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make -B -n` shows `sota_cross_eval.csv` depends on `score_mechanical.py`
- [ ] No sibling rule in score.mk imports a module it does not declare
- [ ] `make check` passes
